3. bring in OWL and OWL reasoning into the stack. [DONE (rule-based scope) - StarLayerGraph.infer(profile="rdfs"|"owl-rl"|"rdfs+owl-rl", mode="full"|"delta"|"in-place") materializes an RDFS/OWL-RL entailment closure (or just the newly-entailed delta, or mutates self directly) via owlrl (docs/guides/02b-graphs-inferencing.ipynb sections 3-3.4). entailment is a per-query choice on .query(), not a graph setting: entailment="rdf" rewrites the query at query time for the SPARQL spec's separate, weaker RDF Entailment regime (just "every predicate used anywhere is rdf:type rdf:Property"); entailment="rdfs" rewrites the query at query time for the full RDFS ruleset (subClassOf/subPropertyOf/domain/range, no data copy); entailment="owl-rl" queries the live union of the graph and a small cached delta (infer(mode="delta")), auto-refreshed on mutation by default, tunable via infer=(changed|always|cached) - composes automatically with a backend that already reasons on its own, since the graph is read live and the delta only contains what wasn't already there (confirmed live against a reasoning-enabled Fuseki dataset, tests/integration/test_entailment_native.py); entailment="native" (backend="rdf-1.2" only) delegates to a reasoning-enabled Fuseki/Jena backend instead - packages/graph/docs/fuseki-reasoning-setup.md documents two verified configs (docs/guides/03b-sparql-inferencing.ipynb, 05b-backend-graph-databases.ipynb section 1.b). infer(profile="owl-dl") adds real OWL 2 DL reasoning via owlready2+Java HermiT (starlayergraph/graph/owl_dl.py) - genuine tableau reasoning, so it derives disjunctive entailments owlrl structurally cannot (e.g. C subClassOf (A or B), not-A(x) |= B(x)), and raises InconsistentOntologyError outright for a logically inconsistent ontology rather than owl-rl's partial, silent err:error triple; owlready2 is a core dependency (installs automatically); a real JVM on PATH is the one prerequisite that isn't (docs/guides/05e-owl-dl-reasoning.ipynb). Remaining g